# Frontend structure

`web/` is React + Vite (npm only). `moduleResolution: bundler`, so a bare
directory import resolves to its `index.{ts,tsx}` — use barrels.

## `web/src/` layout

```
src/
├── api/         # HTTP client + endpoint modules (barrel: api/index.ts)
│   └── client.ts
├── types/       # shared TS types (barrel: types/index.ts)
├── store/       # global store: StoreProvider + useStore (store/index.tsx)
├── lib/         # framework-free utils (lib/format.ts)
├── hooks/       # custom hooks (useStore stays with its Provider in store/)
├── components/  # one folder per component: index.tsx + index.module.scss
├── pages/       # route-level pages (ExaminePage / TeachPage / DrillPage)
├── assets/      # static assets
├── App.tsx
├── main.tsx
└── global.scss
```

## Rules

- **No flat root files** for api/types/store/format — they live in their
  named directories with a barrel `index`. Import as `from "../api"`,
  `from "../types"`, `from "../store"`; the barrel resolves.
- `api/` holds the HTTP client (`api`, `uploadFile`, `fetchBlob` in
  `client.ts`) and, when endpoint helpers accrete, one file per subdomain
  (`day.ts`, `drill.ts`, `resume.ts`, …) re-exported from `api/index.ts`.
  Components call endpoints through these, not raw `fetch`.
- `store/` owns the global context: `StoreProvider` + `useStore` +
  `Store` type, co-located. `useStore` is **not** moved to `hooks/` because it
  is bound to its Provider.
- `lib/` is framework-free pure utils (date/format/html helpers). No React
  imports here.
- `hooks/` is for reusable React hooks shared across components. A hook
  coupled to a single Provider stays with that Provider.
- `components/<Name>/` = `index.tsx` + `index.module.scss` (CSS Modules, no
  global class names). Group into `components/{chat,drill,resume,common}/`
  only when the flat list grows unwieldy.
- `pages/` are route-level shells that compose components + `useStore`.
- Keep subdomain naming aligned with the backend (`day`, `note`, `drill`,
  `resume`, `project`, `memory`, `prompt`) so frontend `api/<domain>.ts`
  maps 1:1 to backend `api/routes/<domain>.py` + `db/ops/<domain>.py`.

## When adding a feature

1. Types → `types/index.ts` (or a domain file re-exported by the barrel).
2. Endpoint helper → `api/<domain>.ts` (re-export from `api/index.ts`); fall
   back to `api<T>("/v1/...")` inline only for one-off calls.
3. Reusable hook → `hooks/`; component → `components/<Name>/`.
4. Page shell → `pages/<Name>Page/`.
